WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.178 --> 00:00:02.761
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.720
- Hi, friends, it's Inga.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.360
I recently heard about this
place called The Dream Machine.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.360
It calls itself a new immersive experience

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.910
that brings the most
magical dreams to life.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.590
We're supposed to walk through 10 rooms

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:18.660
that are inspired by our sleep cycle.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.549
I have absolutely no idea what that means,

00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:22.496
but we're just gonna go to the location,

00:00:22.496 --> 00:00:25.240
check it out, and have some fun.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.250
- I'm Paige Solomon.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.140
I'm the co-founder and creative
director of Dream Machine.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.830
Dream Machine was inspired by sleep dreams

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.260
and the whimsical nature of dreaming.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.660
We wanted to create a space
that was a respite from reality.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:42.310
You'll find yourself walking
through a cloud land on Cloud 9

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.300
and that is the first
point in which each guest

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.860
will really be falling asleep.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.480
- There's a lot of clouds in here.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.863
Look at all these lights.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.810
This looks like what it
would be if I was dreaming.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.470
We tend to forget about our dreams,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.913
so this is kind of like reliving it.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.520
It's a very surreal feeling.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.670
You don't really see anything like this

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.740
outside of this space.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.770
I do actually feel a little bit sleepy,

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.360
which I think is kind of the point.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.782
I think the feeling it
gives you is very much like

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:17.350
how I remember feeling from a dream.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:20.570
I'm feeling great, I have
my head in the clouds.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.600
Literally.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.650
- [Paige] Soon as you're asleep,

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.100
you enter a fog bubble machine,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.970
and that's really your first transition

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.773
into this dream world.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.280
- Holy moly, this is blowin' my mind.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.920
I thought they were bubbles,
but they dissolve into smoke.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.230
You know how in dreams things
don't really make sense?

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.120
This is like that.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.451
Bubbles that turn into smoke?

00:01:47.451 --> 00:01:49.040
That's so bizarre.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.240
I feel like a wish.
(blowing)

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.050
A little bit too wet here.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:57.040
This is the part where I think
I wet my bed in my dream.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.230
- [Paige] From there, you walk
into a black and white room

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.730
because some people only
dream in black and white.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
- That's scary looking.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.030
I've never dreamed in black and white,

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:09.983
but if I did, this would
probably be a nightmare for me.

00:02:17.707 --> 00:02:18.540
(laughing)

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.820
- [Paige] And then the
black and white room

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.330
starts to transition black and white tiles

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.593
into a neon-lit laundromat.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.440
- I'm making cotton candy
out of a washing machine.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.860
Better than any cotton
candy I've ever tasted

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:35.740
out of a washing machine.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.510
- [Paige] In the laundromat
you can crawl through dryers

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.910
into an infinity room.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.160
- Check this out.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.483
There's a lot of little lights in here.

00:02:46.813 --> 00:02:48.983
I feel like I'm in a mini galaxy,

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.683
really serene, quiet.

00:03:07.327 --> 00:03:08.160
What?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:08.993
Well, that was trippy.

00:03:08.993 --> 00:03:10.810
I just came out of a washing machine.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:11.673
Movin' on.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:18.380
- [Paige] From there you'll
find yourself diving underwater

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.780
into a ball pit swimming pool

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.443
that looks like you're at the
bottom of a swimming pool.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.133
- Steps to the pool.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.710
I am in a sea of plastic balls.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.150
I love the watery wavy
patterns on the ceiling.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.700
We're just chillin' underwater.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.013
I never wanna get out now.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.270
- [Paige] From there, that transition

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:46.420
is a 40 foot long rainbow hall.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.793
- We are in the rainbow room.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.550
You can see the colors changing.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:53.923
It is trippy.

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:58.100
I feel like Alice in Alice in Wonderland.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.833
Going down the rabbit hole now.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.560
Will I find a pot of gold
at the end of the rainbow?

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.693
I wonder.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.830
- [Paige] You then find yourself

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.070
immersed in our print garden,

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:11.640
a room filled with 70 plants

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.610
with all different prints, patterns.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:17.490
- I feel like I'm at a fancy rainforest.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.190
These plants have little shapes on it.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.684
A polka dot leaf, there's striped leaves

00:04:22.684 --> 00:04:26.820
and then there's mac and cheese leaves.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.910
It can be whatever you
want, it's your dream.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.160
- [Paige] And then it's time to wake up.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.750
You'll find yourself immersed in 15 feet

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.583
of metallic streamers.
- We're goin' in.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.803
Is this ever going to end?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.413
I feel like I've been here for forever,

00:04:48.791 --> 00:04:51.550
(gasps) and we're out.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.883
It was all a dream.

00:04:56.669 --> 00:04:57.760
Ta-da!

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.140
I feel like I'm waking up.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:02.880
Now that we've finished the entire tour,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.030
I finally know what the dream machine is.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.610
It was actually pretty cool.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.820
There were so many room
that I honestly felt

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.020
like I was in my dream.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:14.913
So, after all that, back to reality it is.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:18.805
Actually, never mind.

00:05:18.805 --> 00:05:20.398
Bye, guys.

00:05:20.398 --> 00:05:23.148
(relaxing music)

